Task: meanAbsoluteDeviation
For a given list of input numbers, calculate the Mean Absolute Deviation around the mean of the dataset: the average absolute difference between each element and the mean.

Definitions (Lean):
@[reducible, simp]
def meanAbsoluteDeviation_precond (numbers : List ℚ) : Prop :=
  numbers ≠ []

@[reducible, simp]
def meanAbsoluteDeviation_postcond (numbers : List ℚ) (result: ℚ) (h_precond : meanAbsoluteDeviation_precond (numbers)) :=
  |result - (numbers.map (fun x => |x - numbers.sum / (numbers.length : ℚ)|)).sum / (numbers.length : ℚ)| ≤ (1 / 1000000 : ℚ)

Goal 1: find ρ : ℚ
numbers : List ℚ
h_precond : meanAbsoluteDeviation_precond numbers
⊢ ∃ ρ, meanAbsoluteDeviation_postcond numbers ρ h_precond

